  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inclusive Programming in Practice: Disability Mainstreaming Pilot</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD is deepening its work on inclusive programming, linked to the SADI Framework. This project with CBM UK will strengthen CAFOD&apos;s practical capacity to embed disability inclusion into its programming from a mainstreaming perspective. It will consist of three parts. Firstly, it will conduct a pilot with the Nigeria CAFOD office to conduct a disability audit, mentor and support key staff to embed disability inclusion throughout the project cycle, and to evidence though an in depth partner example (partner funding is separate).  Secondly, case study collection and ongoing learning examples will contribute to a deep dive training module which will be applied within the SADI material. Wider dissemination of learnings at organisational level is intended to increase awareness and openness to inclusion at all levels of work. Lastly, CBM UK will provide a helpdesk facility which will be on offer for all CAFOD staff to strengthen their skillset and knowledge on disability inclusion in a relevant area of work.</narrative>
  </description>
